        "field_id": "question_19835423004",
        "label": "Why do you want to join Figma?",
        "type": "textarea",
        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:question_19835423004",
        "action": "fill",
        "value": "I want to work on data problems where there is a real product and real users on the other end, and Figma has both. The Data team sitting directly with product and engineering is the part that matters to me. Most of my work has been in that overlap. I built ClarityAtlas end to end in Swift and SwiftUI and shipped it into a live Hopkins pilot with 30+ users, including a passive sleep-estimation system that used step count, gait speed, and motion patterns instead of requiring a wearable, and the hardest part was not the modeling but figuring out what people would actually act on. At Summer Atlantic Capital I work on the ML core of an anomaly-detection system, and the lesson there has been similar: a detector that fires too often creates a second problem instead of solving the first, so ranking and explanation quality decide whether anyone uses it. I also like that Figma's product is a tool people work inside all day, which means behavioral data is dense and the questions are about how people actually collaborate. The part I would want to work on is turning that into measurement someone can make a decision from.",
